  "lineage": "The ceremonial and social music of the Wixárika (Huichol) of the Sierra Madre Occidental in Jalisco and Nayarit, comprising the shaman-mara'akame's long night-long chanted narrations accompanied by the tepu log drum and the xaweri/kanari — a locally built miniature violin and five-string guitar pair — whose 'minuete' dance pieces run in a bright 3/4 with fast bowed ostinati at peyote and maize ceremonies, unnotated and transmitted entirely by apprenticeship.",
